[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":97},"routes/item",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10},"item",{"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":-5,"_20":21,"_22":23,"_24":25,"_26":27,"_28":27,"_29":30,"_31":32,"_33":34,"_35":36,"_37":38,"_39":-5,"_40":-5,"_41":42,"_43":44,"_45":46,"_47":48,"_49":50,"_51":52,"_53":36,"_54":55,"_56":-5,"_57":36,"_58":59},"expiresAt",1795308037000,"id","nios0423zfv9l5e7fe1nvkxig","title","CISA 将 Cisco Expressway、SAP NetWeaver、VMware vCenter 和 Apache Roller 漏洞加入 KEV 目录","originalTitle","U.S. CISA adds Cisco Expressway, SAP NetWeaver, Broadcom VMware vCenter, and Apache Roller flaws to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog","summary","CISA 将 CVE-2025-42884、CVE-2026-76466、CVE-2026-123890 和 CVE-2026-129448 加入 KEV 目录，确认这些漏洞已在真实攻击中使用。","reason","source",{"_68":96},"links",{"_59":95},"publishedAt","2026-11-21T16:09:38.000Z","discoveredAt","2026-11-21T17:52:54.509Z","timelineAt","category","vuln","tags",[69,89,90,72,91,92,74,93,94],"score",88,"selected",false,"channel","news","story","x","readingMode","full","author","Pierluigi Paganini","body",{"_85":-5,"_59":86,"_87":-5,"_88":36},"outline",[79],"relatedStories",[],"topics",[60,61,62,63,64,65],"indexable","markdownAvailable",true,"group","hasTranslation","bodyLanguage","original",{"_66":77,"_68":78},{"_66":75,"_68":76},{"_66":73,"_68":74},{"_66":71,"_68":72},{"_66":30,"_68":70},{"_66":67,"_68":69},"slug","exploited","name","在野利用","漏洞披露","vuln-mgmt","漏洞管理","cisa","CISA","vmware","VMware / Broadcom","cisco","Cisco / 思科",{"_11":80,"_81":82,"_83":84},"sec-1","text","U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) adds Cisco Expressw","level",2,"zh","<h2 id=\"sec-1\">U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) adds Cisco Expressway, SAP NetWeaver, Broadcom VMware vCenter, and Apache Roller flaws to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog.</h2><p>The U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA)&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2026/11/20/cisa-adds-four-known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog\">added</a> Cisco Expressway, SAP NetWeaver, Broadcom VMware vCenter, and Apache Roller vulnerabilities to its&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog\">Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog</a>:</p><ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2025-42884\"><u>CVE-2025-42884</u></a> SAP NetWeaver Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Data Query Logic Vulnerability</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-76466\"><u>CVE-2026-76466</u></a> Cisco Expressway Series Use of Hard-coded Credentials Vulnerability</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-123890\"><u>CVE-2026-123890</u></a> VMWare vCenter Authentication Bypass Using an Alternate Path or Channel Vulnerability</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-129448\"><u>CVE-2026-129448</u></a> Apache Roller Deserialization of Untrusted Data Vulnerability</li>\n</ul><p>The first vulnerability added to the catalog is <strong>CVE-2025-42884</strong> <strong>(CVSS score of 6.5)</strong>, affecting SAP NetWeaver Enterprise Portal. The flaw allows an unauthenticated attacker to inject JNDI environment properties or provide a URL used during JNDI lookup operations. This could give the attacker access to an unintended JNDI provider and allow them to disclose or modify server information. CISA added the vulnerability to its KEV catalog on November 20, 2026, confirming that it has been exploited in the wild. However, no public reports have identified the attackers or provided details about the campaigns in which they used the flaw. </p><p>The second vulnerability is <strong><a href=\"https://securityaffairs.com/203598/hacking/hackers-exploit-cisco-expressway-flaw-cve-2026-76466-to-breach-russian-organization.html\">CVE-2026-76466</a></strong> <strong>(CVSS score of 9.8)</strong>, a critical flaw affecting Cisco Expressway Series. The vulnerability involves hard-coded credentials and insufficient validation of client certificates in clustered deployments. An attacker who obtains persistent cookies can connect to the device’s database service and execute specific remote procedure calls, potentially running arbitrary operating system commands with root privileges. According to cybersecurity firm F6, attackers exploited the flaw to breach clustered Cisco Expressway devices at a Russian organization shortly after a public proof-of-concept exploit became available. They then prepared tools for lateral movement across the victim’s network and accessed sensitive information. The activity has not been attributed to a known threat actor. </p><p>The third vulnerability is <strong>CVE-2026-123890</strong> <strong>(CVSS score of 9.8)</strong>, an authentication bypass affecting VMware vCenter. The flaw resides in the VMware Directory Service and allows an attacker with network access to bypass authentication and gain unauthorized access to the system. Google Threat Intelligence Group and Mandiant linked its exploitation to <strong>ARMORY CASTLE</strong>, a suspected China-nexus cyber espionage group previously tracked as UNC5221. According to their investigation, the group exploited the vulnerability as a zero-day in early September 2026, before Broadcom disclosed and patched it. The attackers used a custom tool named BONESAW to obtain sensitive vCenter data, hijack the SAML Security Token Service and create an administrator account for persistent access. The campaign also involved the exploitation of a BeyondTrust Remote Support vulnerability, CVE-2026-102764. </p><p>The fourth vulnerability is <strong><a href=\"https://securityaffairs.com/203419/security/apache-roller-rce-flaw-cve-2026-129448-under-active-attack.html\">CVE-2026-129448</a></strong> <strong>(CVSS score of 9.8)</strong>, a critical deserialization flaw affecting Apache Roller versions 4.0.0 through 6.1.4. The issue affects the XML-RPC endpoint, which accepts and deserializes vendor extension types before authenticating requests. An unauthenticated remote attacker can exploit this behavior to execute arbitrary code on a vulnerable server. The Apache Roller maintainers have confirmed that attackers are exploiting the vulnerability in the wild, and CISA has added it to the KEV catalog. However, neither the project maintainers nor public reports have identified the threat actors behind these attacks or provided details about their targets and objectives. </p><p>According to&nbsp;<a href=\"https://cyber.dhs.gov/bod/22-01/\">Binding Operational Directive (BOD) 22-01: Reducing the Significant Risk of Known Exploited Vulnerabilities</a>, FCEB agencies have to address the identified vulnerabilities by the due date to protect their networks against attacks exploiting the flaws in the catalog.</p><p>Experts also recommend that private organizations review the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog\">Catalog</a>&nbsp;and address the vulnerabilities in their infrastructure.</p><p>CISA orders federal agencies to fix the vulnerabilities by November 23.</p><p><strong>Follow me on Twitter:&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://twitter.com/securityaffairs\"><strong>@securityaffairs</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/sec.affairs\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://infosec.exchange/@securityaffairs\"><strong>Mastodon</strong></a><strong></strong></p><p><a href=\"http://www.linkedin.com/pub/pierluigi-paganini/b/742/559\"><strong>Pierluigi&nbsp;Paganini</strong></a><strong></strong></p><p><strong>(</strong><a href=\"http://securityaffairs.co/wordpress/\"><strong>SecurityAffairs</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;–&nbsp;hacking,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://securityaffairs.com/tag/cisa\">CISA</a>)</strong></p>","zhKind","complete","补丁","漏洞","Cisco","Google","Oracle","VMware","https://securityaffairs.com/203639/security/u-s-cisa-adds-cisco-expressway-sap-netweaver-broadcom-vmware-vcenter-and-apache-roller-flaws-to-its-known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog.html","Security Affairs",{"_98":99,"_100":-5},"changelogVersion","2026-10-01T08:00","release"]
